  itemDescription: Environmental Protection Technologies Institute  This institute
    focuses on pollution control and ecological conservation technologies. Its mission
    covers developing methods to prevent or mitigate pollution of air, water, and
    soil, as well as protecting biodiversity. Key research areas include emissions
    reduction (e.g. scrubbers, filters for factories), treatment of agricultural
    and industrial run-off, remediation of contaminated sites, and monitoring environmental
    quality. The institute also works on ecosystem restoration and wildlife protection
    technologies, aligning with initiatives like preserving natural reserves. By
    advancing these technologies, the institute aims to safeguard environmental health
    and comply with environmental regulations and standards
